  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $8-2z$ whose distance from zero is greater than $2.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-2z & <-2 & \\text{or} &  & 8-2z & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-2z & <-2 &  &  & 8-2z & >2 \\\\ -2z & <-10 &  &  & -2z & >-6 \\\\ z & >5 &  &  & z & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z<3 &  & \\text{or} &  & z>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
